   {
    "id": "a1",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "Body: 1-junction of the lunar module. Inertia = modulated spatial I (m(t), J(m)); Out1..6 = MR on the joint's drive axes (1-junctions Axis1..6), r = -dm/dt and -dJ/dt: the propellant that leaves takes its momentum with it.",
    "x": 400,
    "y": 60,
    "w": 560,
    "h": 60
   },
   {
    "id": "a2",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "Landing gear: four footpads (167.57 in from the X axis, TN D-6850), each an instance of the library subsystem LunarFoot: a ContactPoint (Hunt-Crossley normal force for pad, strut and soil; Coulomb friction mu = 0.4) on the lunar sphere below it (LunarSurface3D), mounted at its pad through a FixedTransform3DNeutral.",
    "x": 1000,
    "y": 1100,
    "w": 780,
    "h": 60
   },
   {
    "id": "a3",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "Landing phase (P66, rate of descent) by hand: start in a hover, set the descent rate above and below 100 ft and a forward translation on the dashboard, and land before the propellant runs out.",
    "x": 40,
    "y": -40,
    "w": 960,
    "h": 60
   }
  ]
